                    <note type="editorial">Joseph  Fiévée was a publisher during the French Revolution. He was imprisoned for his royalist sympathies but seems to have been released from custody by 
    <persName key="NAP02">Napoleon</persName> who sent him to 
    Britain during the peace of Amiens to spy.  
    Fiévée
  was openly gay and Godwin met with him and his partner, <persName key="LEC01">Théodore LeClercq</persName>.  They were accompanied by Fiévée's son.</note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"> Jeremy D. Popkin, <title>Joseph Fiévée, imprimeur, écrivain, journaliste: une carrière dans le monde du livre pendant la Révolution</title>, 1988</bibl>
